import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Handl Compile Plugin Architecture","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Handl Compile Plugin Architecture","type":"adr","date":"2026-09-14T00:00:00.000Z","status":"proposed","status_note":"Proposed."},"headers":[],"relativePath":"handl/project/adrs/0114-handl-compile-plugin-architecture.md","filePath":"vendored/handl/project/adrs/0114-handl-compile-plugin-architecture.md"}`),a={name:`handl/project/adrs/0114-handl-compile-plugin-architecture.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="adr-0114-handl-compile-plugin-architecture" tabindex="-1">ADR-0114: Handl Compile Plugin Architecture <a class="header-anchor" href="#adr-0114-handl-compile-plugin-architecture" aria-label="Permalink to “ADR-0114: Handl Compile Plugin Architecture”">​</a></h1><h2 id="context" tabindex="-1">Context <a class="header-anchor" href="#context" aria-label="Permalink to “Context”">​</a></h2><p>Handl currently has three execution engines (tree-walk, bytecode, cranelift) that run Handl source at compile time and at runtime. It also has <code>handl-emitters</code> for emitting <code>Language</code> data fragments and <code>plugin-sdkgen-emitter-file</code> for writing generated SDK <code>.hnl</code> files. What it does <strong>not</strong> have is a generic plugin architecture for compiling Handl source to external target languages such as JavaScript, C, or WebAssembly.</p><h2 id="decision" tabindex="-1">Decision <a class="header-anchor" href="#decision" aria-label="Permalink to “Decision”">​</a></h2><p>Introduce a <code>plugin-compile</code> family of crates.</p><ul><li><code>plugin-compile</code> defines a <code>Compiler</code> trait and the target-agnostic <code>CompilerInput</code> (a parsed and type-checked Handl <code>Ast</code> plus optional metadata).</li><li>Per-target compiler crates implement <code>Compiler</code>: <ul><li><code>plugin-compile-js</code> — emits JavaScript for browser / Deno / Node.</li><li><code>plugin-compile-llvm</code> — emits native code and object files.</li></ul></li><li>The existing <code>handl-emitters</code> crate keeps its current role: emitting <code>Language</code> data fragments. It is <strong>not</strong> a source-to-source compiler.</li><li><code>host-cli</code> gains a <code>hnl compile &lt;target&gt; &lt;file&gt;</code> subcommand that dispatches to the appropriate compiler plugin.</li><li>Compilers are selected by target name, not by file extension. The target triple / runtime is part of the compiler configuration.</li></ul><h3 id="javascript-target" tabindex="-1">JavaScript target <a class="header-anchor" href="#javascript-target" aria-label="Permalink to “JavaScript target”">​</a></h3><p><code>plugin-compile-js</code> implements <code>Compiler</code> for JavaScript. It provides:</p><ul><li><code>compile_to_string(input, config) -&gt; Result&lt;String, CompileError&gt;</code> — lower the type-checked <code>Ast</code> to a single generated JS string.</li><li><code>emit_module(input, out_dir) -&gt; Result&lt;JsOutputManifest, CompileError&gt;</code> — write one or more <code>.js</code> / <code>.mjs</code> files plus a runtime manifest.</li><li><code>runtime_prelude(runtime) -&gt; String</code> — choose the <code>browser</code>, <code>deno</code>, or <code>node</code> shim.</li></ul><p><code>JsConfig.output_mode</code> controls output form:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Mode</th><th>Use case</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>esm</code></td><td>ECMAScript modules; default for Deno and modern browsers.</td></tr><tr><td><code>commonjs</code></td><td><code>require</code> / <code>module.exports</code>; for Node.</td></tr><tr><td><code>inline</code></td><td>Self-contained <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> or <code>eval</code> string.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Value lowering: Handl primitives map to JS primitives; <code>Arr</code>/<code>Obj</code> become JS arrays/objects; <code>Bytes</code> becomes <code>Uint8Array</code>; <code>Handle</code>/<code>Resource</code> becomes an opaque reference; <code>Pair</code> and <code>Either</code> use tagged shapes; arrows become JS closures. Foreign calls lower to the <code>js</code> client package from ADR-0113: <code>js.call(&quot;&lt;module&gt;.&lt;name&gt;&quot;, args)</code> with <code>js.errno()</code> for errors. The runtime shim registers host functions by <code>(module, name)</code> so WebIDL/foreign binding metadata can be shared.</p><p><code>plugin-compile-js</code> inlines <code>js.call</code> / <code>js.error</code> by default when the foreign object, method, and descriptors are known at compile time. For example, <code>call(&quot;console&quot;, &quot;log&quot;, [msg], [&quot;js_string&quot;], &quot;js_void&quot;, false)</code> compiles directly to <code>console.log(msg)</code>. A configuration flag (<code>--no-inline-foreign</code> or <code>keep_js_shim</code>) opts out of inlining and keeps the runtime <code>js</code> client package for dynamic or generic foreign calls.</p><p><strong>Consequences for the JS target:</strong> v1 does not emit source maps; stack traces point at generated JS. The <code>inline</code> and <code>esm</code> modes may include a <code># sourceURL=&lt;input&gt;</code> comment for debugging.</p><p><strong>Open questions:</strong></p><ol><li>Source maps generated by the compiler or by a separate debug crate?</li><li>Bundled <code>handl-runtime.js</code> per target, or granular helper imports?</li></ol><h3 id="llvm-target" tabindex="-1">LLVM target <a class="header-anchor" href="#llvm-target" aria-label="Permalink to “LLVM target”">​</a></h3><p><code>plugin-compile-llvm</code> implements <code>Compiler</code> for native object output using <code>inkwell</code>. It provides:</p><ul><li><code>target() -&gt; &amp;str</code> — returns <code>&quot;llvm&quot;</code>.</li><li><code>compile(input) -&gt; Result&lt;CompilerOutput, CompileError&gt;</code> — build an LLVM module and emit a relocatable <code>.o</code> file.</li><li><code>set_target_triple(triple)</code> — override the default host triple.</li></ul><p>The lowering follows <code>plugin-engine-exec-cranelift</code> (<code>crates/plugin-engine-exec-cranelift/src/compile.rs</code>): each v2 <code>Term</code> compiles to <code>fn(*mut EvalCtx, *mut Value) -&gt; *mut Value</code>; literal and name pools accumulate in constant arrays; every <code>helper_v2_*</code> runtime helper is declared <code>extern &quot;C&quot;</code>. <code>TargetMachine</code> target initialization runs for the requested architecture before the module is built. FFI arrows call <code>helper_v2_call_ffi_raw</code> with the foreign name and descriptor from the name pool.</p><p><code>inkwell</code> is preferred over raw <code>llvm-sys</code> to keep the builder API close to the existing cranelift/emitter patterns and to centralize LLVM lifetime bookkeeping.</p><p><strong>Consequences for the LLVM target:</strong></p><ul><li>Adds a system-LLVM build dependency and an <code>inkwell</code> version coupling.</li><li>Emits object files that must be linked with the Handl runtime helper library, unlike the self-contained cranelift JIT path.</li></ul><p><strong>Open questions:</strong></p><ul><li>Share the exact <code>helper_v2_*</code> ABI with cranelift, or define a slimmer <code>libhandlrt</code>?</li><li>Where is cross-target validation enforced: <code>CompilerInput</code>, CLI, or <code>TargetMachine</code> creation?</li></ul><h2 id="consequences" tabindex="-1">Consequences <a class="header-anchor" href="#consequences" aria-label="Permalink to “Consequences”">​</a></h2><ul><li>Compilers become first-class plugins alongside formatters, linters, and the test runner.</li><li>The <code>Compiler</code> trait can be implemented without touching the Handl core, as long as the input AST and type information are exposed.</li><li>The SDK generator (<code>plugin-sdkgen-*</code>) and the source-to-source compiler (<code>plugin-compile-*</code>) remain separate concerns: the former turns foreign APIs into Handl source; the latter turns Handl source into foreign code.</li><li>A new dependency appears: the compiler needs access to the type-checked AST and a type/grade projection API from <code>plugin-engine-typecheck</code>.</li></ul><h2 id="references" tabindex="-1">References <a class="header-anchor" href="#references" aria-label="Permalink to “References”">​</a></h2><ul><li><a href="./0107-handl-sdk-generator.html">ADR-0107 — Handl SDK Generator</a></li><li><a href="./0090-bootstrap-cli.html">ADR-0090 — Bootstrap CLI</a></li></ul>`,29)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};